  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "The Astros scored three in the eighth and took the division fight with them.",
    "what_this_means": "Luis Garc\u00eda Jr. kept them in it all night. Three RBIs, and a go-ahead double in the seventh that broke a 5\u20135 tie. But then the bullpen fractured. Fernando Cruz gave up two runs in the sixth before the game even mattered. Then Brent Headrick walked into the eighth and surrendered three more. Ten hits is not an offensive failure. Three runs converted on nine RISP situations is respectable, not wasteful. This game belonged to them until the moment it didn't, and by then the math had flipped too far. A lead that lasted two innings is not leadership. It's exposure. They had the moments. The eighth inning had other plans.",
    "what_to_watch": "Houston's Peter Lambert arrives tonight with a 3.68 ERA and one job: do not let the Yankees lineup build early pressure the way Garc\u00eda and Bellinger tried to. The Yankees need answers from a bullpen that just showed exactly what fragile looks like.",
